  "result": "JWT `exp` field = seconds since epoch. `Date.now()` = milliseconds. Off by 1000x.\n\n**Bug:**\n```js\nif (Date.now() > payload.exp) // wrong \u2014 Date.now() always >> exp\n```\n\n**Fix:**\n```js\nif (Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000) > payload.exp) // compare same unit\n```\n\nOr flip it \u2014 check token still valid:\n```js\nif (payload.exp < Math.floor(Date.now() / 1000)) {\n  return res.status(401).json({ error: 'Token expired' });\n}\n```\n\nSide note: if using `jsonwebtoken` library, `jwt.verify()` handles expiry check automatically \u2014 no manual compare needed.",
